<title>LATVIA: VISA-FREE TRAVEL AGREEMENT SIGNED WITH FINLAND.</title>
<headline>VISA-FREE TRAVEL AGREEMENT SIGNED WITH FINLAND.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Latvian Foreign Minister Valdis Birkavs and his Finnish counterpart Tarja Halonena signed an agreement on visa-free travel between the two states on Monday.</p>
<p>Halonena told reporters after the signing that the agreement would benefit both countries and would lead to increased trade and commerce between the two states.</p>
<p>She added that Finland staunchly supported Latvia's bid for European Union membership and was certain that both Latvia and Lithuania would soon be added to the list of states selected for EU entry talks.</p>
<p>The European Commission earlier this month announced that five Eastern European states, including Estonia, were ready to begin membership negotiations with the EU. Latvia and Lithuania were exlcuded.</p>
<p>&quot;We are optimistic that Latvia and Lithuania will also be included on the list soon,&quot; Halonena said.</p>
<p>-- Ed Stoddard, Riga newsroom +371 722 66 93</p>
</text>
